  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `grblhal.cps`, `grbl.cps` and `tinyg.cps` remember the tool that the program last loaded (`loadedTool`). This is the rule that `tormach.cps` has since #1626.\n- When the next section asks for the same tool, the post writes no tool change:\n  - grblHAL: no `T<n> M6`, and no optional `M1` before it.\n  - TinyG: no `M5` / `M9` / `T<n> M6` / `M0` block, and no frame restate after it.\n  - Grbl 1.1: no `TOOL CHANGE - LOAD` comment and no `M0`.\n- A program stop or an optional stop after an operation makes the tool unknown again. The operator can take the tool out at a stop.\n- The tool comment, the Z lift, the section-end `M5` / `M9`, the next `S.. M3` and the Z-only clearance rapid before the first traverse stay.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe three posts wrote a full tool change for each `TOOL` record. The stream sends a `TOOL` record for each section, also when the tool does not change. On a manual-change router, each `M6` (or the Grbl `M0`) halts the program.\n\n## Tests\n\n- New file `crates/post/tests/grbl_family_same_tool.rs`, six tests:\n  - `grblhal_repeated_tool_writes_one_tool_change`\n  - `grblhal_new_tool_return_and_stop_each_change_again`\n  - `grbl_repeated_tool_writes_no_tool_change_stop`\n  - `grbl_new_tool_return_and_stop_each_change_again`\n  - `tinyg_repeated_tool_writes_one_tool_change`\n  - `tinyg_new_tool_return_and_stop_each_change_again`\n- All six were red on unchanged code.\n- Mutations:\n  - `grblhal.cps` from upstream/main: the two grblhal tests are red.\n  - `grbl.cps` from upstream/main: the two grbl tests are red.\n  - `tinyg.cps` from upstream/main: the two tinyg tests are red.\n  - The grblHAL stop reset removed: `grblhal_new_tool_return_and_stop_each_change_again` is red.\n  - Restored: all six are green.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 58 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No recorded stream or app golden has two sections in a row on one tool for these posts.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real grblHAL, Grbl or TinyG controller.\n- The q07 router project was not posted again through the app.\n- The Z lift and the spindle stop and start between same-tool sections stay. The issue asks for them to go too. `docs/decisions/3445-grbl-same-tool.md` says why they stay.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone.\n\nChangelog: The grblHAL, Grbl 1.1 and TinyG posts write no tool change between operations that keep the same tool.\n\nFixes #3445\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
